WEBVTT

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:06.800
Who'd visit this early in the morning?

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.090
I couldn't say. It's quite early for a newspaper salesman.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.590
Hail!

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:14.550
"Hail"?

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:17.010
Sire, could it be...

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:26.980
--The one from the stairs yesterday?
--In all likelihood.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.650
Hail!

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:31.990
Y-Yes?

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.160
Forgive the early hour.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:38.410
I am called Suzuno Kamazuki.
I moved next door yesterday.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.200
I'm afraid not only did I commit a rudeness before we met,

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:43.540
but I caused you trouble. I am most wretched.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:45.250
Wr-Wretched?

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:48.380
Uh, that's very courteous.

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:51.590
Pleased to formally meet you.
My name is Sadao Maou.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:56.260
This is a small token of my thanks and good wishes as your neighbor.

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:59.930
I'm told noodles are the best gift for a new neighbor.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:04.100
R-Right, that's very--<i>kind</i>!

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:07.150
A-Are you all right, Sire?

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.570
--Wh-Why wouldn't I be?
--Er...

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:14.610
Ah, excuse me. My name is Ashiya, and I'm an old friend of Maou's.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:18.450
--A-Ashiya! H-Here, take this!

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:17.370
--I know of you two.

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:20.280
--I have never met the landlady of this establishment,

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:20.290
--Oh, yes.

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:23.660
--but I received a letter from someone I believe to be the landlady
--H-Heavy!

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:27.130
instructing me to come to you with any troubles.

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:28.130
I see...

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:33.380
There was a photograph enclosed--

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:36.680
Yes, yes! That's certainly her.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:42.020
In any case, I'm heartened to have helpful neighbors.

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:45.850
Would you be kind enough to instruct me in tenement house living?

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:48.810
"Tenement house living"?

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:50.320
Is there someone else here?

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:52.570
We gained another roommate recently.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:55.150
I'm Urushihara! Hello neighbor!

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:56.990
"I'm a shut-in!"

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.120
That ain't by choice!

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:01.030
Hmm, why <i>is</i> it?

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:04.160
It's--that's--no--

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:05.660
I see. I get it.

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:07.790
Get what?!

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.340
I'll excuse myself for now. Salutations, and I hope we'll have a good relationship.

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:13.840
S-Salutations.

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:29.520
<i>Right here, this moment,</i> <i>this is our starting point</i>

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:35.570
<i>Let's picture what we might be able to do</i>

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:39.610
<i>Unbelievable things can happen sometimes</i>

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:45.330
<i>More... we can push past this</i>

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:56.210
<i>Everything is born from zero;</i>
<i>I want to shine, flap my wings hard</i>

00:02:57.470 --> 00:03:00.680
<i>And fly to that sky</i>

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:07.850
<i>Come on, let's go, with</i> <i>brilliant smiles on our faces!</i>

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:13.650
<i>Let's fly off to an unknown world right now</i>

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:18.320
<i>I decide, I'm the one who chooses my future</i>

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:20.700
<i>Let's follow our dreams</i>

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:22.240
<i>Sure, some days we'll cry</i>

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:28.540
<i>It's a precious wish, don't disappear</i>

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:36.460
<i>I'm going after the future you,</i> <i>because I know I'll find you</i>

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:52.770
Hello!

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:56.820
--This is Emerada Etuva!
--I know that.

00:03:57.030 --> 00:03:59.900
This is Yusa--I mean, Emilia.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:03.950
I got a package that says it's from you. What is this thing?

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:10.960
Oh, so it arrived? That's amazing!
I only just sent it yesterday!

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:13.290
Talk about fast!

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.590
It's celestial force!

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:17.420
Huh? Celestial force?

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:24.720
I processed it into a form that wouldn't seem out of the ordinary in Japan!

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:27.470
Eugh, "Holyvitan B"?

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:30.100
That's not a "b," it's a "ß"!

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:34.810
Whatever, but basically you're saying if I drink this, I can replenish my force?

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:40.610
That's right! But be very careful about the dosage!

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:43.820
Dosage? Is there a standard one or something?

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:49.660
Yep, please consider two bottles a day to be the maximum!

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:53.160
You take one in the morning and one in the afternoon,

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:58.380
but if you skip the morning dose, you can't double up in the afternoon!

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:01.210
Right... Okay, understood.

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:07.050
Great! Please use it exactly according to the instructions!

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:08.810
Bye now!

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:11.980
Where <i>is</i> that girl, anyway?

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:15.440
Well, nothing ventured, nothing gained.

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:25.150
Why is the weather always so hot?

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:28.530
And those guys aren't up to much...

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:31.790
I feel like I'm sweating for nothing...

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:37.880
It's all about perspective!

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:43.460
It's <i>good</i> that they're just working and eating like normal people, right? Peaceful!

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:51.470
But from some perspectives, this makes me a stalker

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:55.690
lurking around a peaceful all-male household, huh...

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:02.820
Honestly! Can you not adequately hang one piece of laundry?

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:05.530
You truly know nothing of chores, do you, good Hanzo?

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:07.610
Ugh, lay off.

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:10.450
If you let clothes dry wrinkled, they won't keep their shape.

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:12.660
--They will also dry unevenly.
--Hmm? Who's that?

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:14.700
Yeah, yeah, so sorry.

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:18.880
Jeez, you're seriously like a second Ashiya.

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:21.460
--What?! What's going on?!
--You're tiresomely lazy.

00:06:21.670 --> 00:06:25.630
--Wait... is she a new demon?!
--If you're secluding yourself at home, you ought to at least help with the housework!

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:29.180
This is a little risky, but I've got no choice.

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:34.180
You should get your act together in times of crisis like this.

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:38.980
Listen here. Chop the
Welsh onions, grate the ginger,

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:41.020
and dilute the broth with cold water.

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:44.940
Now if you boil some udon, you have a meal in a flash.

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:45.860
Once they're done,

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:49.160
give them a quick rinse and you have perfectly respectable cold udon.

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:51.490
If we had a raw egg, it would be perfect.

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:55.080
Ugh, you actually boil udon when it's this hot?

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:58.000
The good Shiro does this for three meals every day.

00:06:58.210 --> 00:07:00.920
Do you feel no filial piety?

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:04.460
Please keep at him, Miss Kamazuki.

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:07.130
He won't listen to these things from his own family.

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:09.050
Go on, grate some ginger.

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:11.260
Surely you can at least handle a grater.

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:13.100
Roger...

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:18.980
Huh? Ashiya, are we out of ginger?

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:21.980
Ah, that's right, we used it up yesterday...

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:25.690
I beg your pardon, Miss Kamazuki, but let's just add Welsh onions today.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:26.730
Urushihara!

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:28.650
--What are they even doing?
--No using the refrigerator to cool off!

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:32.450
I shall go fetch some ginger from my room.

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:33.780
Crap!

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:45.210
Are you capable of using the stairs quietly?

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:46.460
M-Maou?!

00:07:46.670 --> 00:07:49.550
Jeez, heroes shouldn't fall down the steps.

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:57.890
What are you two doing?

00:08:01.190 --> 00:08:04.440
I apologize. This is because
I opened the door so suddenly.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:10.320
No, it was nothing you did. It's my fault for not watching my footing.

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:14.160
Yep, totally. And she claims to be a hero...

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:17.870
Yusa! I picked up most of your stuff from outside.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:21.330
Oh, good work. Put it over there.

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:24.210
That high-and-mighty attitude pisses me off.

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:26.420
And what even is this?

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:28.130
You drink health drinks?

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:29.880
Hey!

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:33.180
Drinking that stuff will give you heat fatigue like Ashiya.

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:35.890
What?! You've got heat fatigue?!

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:39.310
I fall ill sometimes, just the same as anyone else.

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:42.310
It seems my gift was to blame.

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:45.560
I should have chosen something more nutritious.

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:49.030
Oh, no, it's not your fault, Miss Kamazuki.

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:51.440
Oh, I haven't introduced myself yet.

00:08:51.650 --> 00:08:57.450
I moved in next door last week.
My name is Suzuno Kamazuki.

00:08:57.660 --> 00:09:01.250
As I come from an ancient and old-fashioned family in a faraway land,

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:04.370
I'm still not well accustomed to Tokyo.

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:06.880
I'd be most happy if you'd instruct me in city life.

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:08.420
I guess we're about the same.

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:10.880
--Hmm?
--Oh, nothing!

00:09:11.090 --> 00:09:13.720
I'm Emi Yusa. Nice to meet you.

00:09:13.930 --> 00:09:15.760
Thanks for the food.

00:09:17.470 --> 00:09:21.890
Man, there's too much to do and memorize. I'm so beat.

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:24.730
Your part-timing isn't anything new.

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:31.440
While you've been lazing through life,
<i>I've</i> greatly matured as a human.

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:33.030
In what way?

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:35.070
And you're not human.

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:38.740
Have you forgotten, Emi?
Just two days from now, on Sunday,

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:42.410
I will become shift manager at the Hatagaya MgRonald's!

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:44.160
The deputy boss!

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:44.960
Uh-huh.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:47.080
Hey! You don't believe me, do you?!

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:51.250
Shift managers get extra pay and a position of responsibility!

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:56.010
What's hardest to believe is you genuinely bragging about that to me.

00:09:56.220 --> 00:10:01.470
Well, fine. Eventually I'll claw my way up to heights <i>you</i> can't even imagine!

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:04.270
--Are you an idiot?
--Hey, Yusa!

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:07.190
I cannot allow you to speak to the head of our household...

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:09.060
--in that way...
--What?

00:10:09.270 --> 00:10:13.610
Good Emi, do you perchance have a very close relationship with good Sadao?

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:14.940
Huh?!

00:10:15.150 --> 00:10:16.450
That's not funny!

00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:19.620
Well... It's just that your conversation flows so easily,

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:24.290
or rather, there seems to be no restraint in your relationship...

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:26.290
Well, that's certainly one way to put it.

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:28.620
Don't you butt in!

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:30.540
We don't feel restraint, but more importantly,

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:34.050
we don't feel trust, or friendship, or anything positive <i>at all</i>!

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:39.220
In fact, I pretty seriously want him to drop dead, so let's get that clear.

00:10:39.430 --> 00:10:41.140
I-I see...

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:44.850
I feel like I've seen this situation before...

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:51.650
I-I'm sure I'm reading this wrong, but are you after Maou too?

00:10:54.190 --> 00:10:55.820
Wh-What are you--?

00:10:56.860 --> 00:10:58.990
Wh-What if he overheard?!

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:03.450
Huh? Oh... I'm sorry.
I really didn't think you were.

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:06.450
B-Be that as it may, I'm impressed.

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:07.960
What tipped you off?

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:10.620
I can't really explain it...

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:17.670
I'd better not say I've been through this before.

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:20.300
I just had a hunch, that's all!

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:22.720
I see. Impressive...

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:28.180
At first I thought she was an assassin from Ente Isla, or a new demon,

00:11:28.390 --> 00:11:32.520
but it'd be odd for an assassin not to make a move for a whole week,

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:35.480
and for a demon, she's too polite to me.

00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:37.940
Maybe I should give her a warning.

00:11:38.150 --> 00:11:42.870
Say, Suzuno. You might think this is none of my business, but listen.

00:11:43.070 --> 00:11:44.030
What is it?

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:48.540
You shouldn't get too close to him.
It'll only end badly for you.

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:50.540
What do you mean?

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:54.090
He's not the kind of man a normal person can handle.

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:57.000
It's best to steer clear if you can.

00:11:57.210 --> 00:12:02.090
B-But--I may not look it, but I'm a seasoned warrior!

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:06.430
Still... Since this is coming from <i>you</i>, I'll take care.

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:10.140
There must be something about him that only you know.

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:14.230
Nevertheless, it's too late for me to leave.

00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:18.070
I realize this is impertinent, but would you lend me your aid?

00:12:18.280 --> 00:12:20.530
Sure, if I can.

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:23.740
You will? Then I can rest a little easier.

00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:25.870
I have an idea. Wait here a sec.

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:32.160
You didn't get up to any funny business while I was gone, did you?

00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:34.830
I value my life more than that.

00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:39.670
This is my cell number, email, and home address.

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:43.970
If these guys say anything awful to you, ask for my help anytime.

00:12:44.180 --> 00:12:45.970
Understood. I'm in your debt.

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:48.970
What do you think we are?

00:12:49.180 --> 00:12:52.100
Bloodthirsty demons more despicable than cockroaches.

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:54.850
I'm sure I don't have to say this, but FYI, if you pull anything with Suzuno

00:12:55.060 --> 00:12:57.940
I'll cut off your head and display it on that windowsill.

00:12:58.150 --> 00:13:00.030
Are you the evil sheriff now?

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:02.950
Okay, I'm off.

00:13:03.150 --> 00:13:07.620
Don't worry, though. They're a more law-abiding bunch than they look.

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:09.200
See you later!

00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:19.960
I-I'm okay. I'm okay this time! Really...

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:23.550
She clear the K-point?

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:26.300
No, she saved herself from going all the way.

00:13:26.510 --> 00:13:28.050
Seems like it.

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:30.390
Ow, ow, ow...

00:13:40.150 --> 00:13:41.690
Okay, I'm going.

00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:44.240
May the tides of war be with you.

00:13:44.450 --> 00:13:47.360
Don't worry about seeing me off, just stay in bed.

00:13:47.570 --> 00:13:50.700
Dealing with Emi totally saps my energy.

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:52.540
Good Sadao.

00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:56.330
Oh, Miss Kamazuki. Sorry about before.

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:59.290
Did she say anything rude to you?

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:01.710
No, nothing rude...

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:03.210
All right, then.

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:05.130
Well, I'm off to work.

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:07.470
Um, here. For you.

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:08.590
Pardon?

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:14.350
So, how's the Holyvitan ß working?

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:20.230
Well, I'm drinking it, but I haven't had the chance to see any real effects.

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:22.940
There haven't been any battles or anything lately.

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:28.200
Oh? So how are you getting on with the Devil these days, then?

00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:32.870
The same as ever. We basically fight whenever we see each other,

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:36.960
and we're both so busy with work we don't have the energy for personal lives.

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:43.130
You know, that's a typical complaint of couples with not enough time together.

00:14:43.340 --> 00:14:46.670
Wh-Where did <i>that</i> come from, Eme?!

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:49.510
I'm Ente Isla's hero and he's the Devil!

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:51.850
He's my enemy, whatever situation we're in!

00:14:52.050 --> 00:14:56.270
C-C-C-<i>Couple</i>?! It makes me furious just to think about it!

00:14:56.480 --> 00:14:58.940
I was keeping <i>tabs</i> on him this morning, and that's what I'm doing now!

00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:02.730
--How can you suggest that when you aren't even looking at us?!
--I know, I know.

00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:10.820
Just please, Emilia, don't do anything to set us against each other, okay?

00:15:11.030 --> 00:15:13.370
Don't worry, I'm a hero!

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:17.370
I swear on my mother's and father's names that I won't make any mistakes.

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:19.580
So, how are things over there?

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:25.840
Well, none of the countries have made any obvious moves.

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:28.010
Any <i>obvious</i> moves.

00:15:28.220 --> 00:15:31.090
Yes, that's right.

00:15:31.300 --> 00:15:33.850
I hear all sorts of information,

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:37.220
but right now it's all just rumors.

00:15:37.430 --> 00:15:38.140
Also...

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:39.270
Also?

00:15:39.480 --> 00:15:41.400
I heard that the Church's Missionary Division

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:45.940
is trying to uncover the truth behind Olba's disappearance.

00:15:46.150 --> 00:15:51.410
It's possible that some may set their sights on trying to find you, too.

00:15:51.610 --> 00:15:55.830
Either way, please don't let your guard down.

00:15:56.040 --> 00:15:58.910
Some of them may be the sort that would be willing to

00:15:59.120 --> 00:16:02.370
cause trouble for Japan in order to quickly achieve their goals, so...

00:16:02.580 --> 00:16:06.000
I guess heroes can't ever catch a break, huh?

00:16:06.210 --> 00:16:08.010
Seems like it.

00:16:08.210 --> 00:16:13.470
Well then... We'll rack up a big bill if we're on the phone too long,

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:15.300
so I'm gonna hang up now.

00:16:15.510 --> 00:16:18.010
Okay. Later, then.

00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:22.020
As you know, tomorrow a restaurant that is expected to pose a major threat to us,

00:16:22.230 --> 00:16:25.190
Sentucky Fried Chicken, will finally be open for business.

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:31.650
I'll be out tomorrow afternoon, so I'll be counting on you to run the ship, Maa.

00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:32.490
Yes, Ma'am!

00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:34.320
Of course, in case there's an emergency,

00:16:34.530 --> 00:16:36.780
I'll make arrangements so that you can reach me at any time.

00:16:36.990 --> 00:16:41.540
But unless it's really serious, go ahead and handle things on your own.

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:43.960
This is also for your personal growth.

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:45.040
Okay!

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:48.050
There aren't many people working tonight, so don't let your guard down.

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:51.550
Consider your job as a shift manager to have already begun.

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:52.380
What?

00:16:52.550 --> 00:16:55.680
At any rate, take a break now while you can.

00:16:55.890 --> 00:16:59.260
If you're gonna come back by 18:00, you can go have dinner.

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:01.980
Or would you like to have some free MgRonald's for dinner?

00:17:02.180 --> 00:17:04.600
I brought my dinner today, so...

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:08.730
Oh, Mr. Maou, are you taking a break?

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:11.530
Yeah, I thought I'd have dinner.

00:17:13.950 --> 00:17:15.820
Mr. Maou... is that...

00:17:16.030 --> 00:17:17.740
This? It's a lunch box.

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:22.290
A lunch box...? That's sort of a simple but elegant lunch box.

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:24.750
Did Mr. Ashiya splurge on that?

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:26.250
No, I'm borrowing it.

00:17:26.460 --> 00:17:30.460
To tell you the truth, a neighbor recently moved in next door.

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:33.670
Next door...? You mean in <i>that</i> apartment house?

00:17:33.880 --> 00:17:36.090
Yeah, it's a young lady.

00:17:36.300 --> 00:17:38.010
A-A lady?!

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:40.600
Don't suddenly start shouting like that!

00:17:40.810 --> 00:17:44.140
A-A lady...?! You borrowed her lunch box...?!

00:17:44.350 --> 00:17:45.940
What's this all about?!

00:17:46.150 --> 00:17:48.110
Chi! Don't shake me! Don't shake me!

00:17:48.310 --> 00:17:52.440
I-I-In other words, um... t-t-the lady next door lent it t-t-to you, Mr. Maou...?!

00:17:52.650 --> 00:17:55.610
Th-Th-That's right. Please stop shaking me!

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:57.990
I'm sure... I'm sure it's not the case...

00:17:58.200 --> 00:18:00.080
I'm sure it's not the case...!

00:18:00.280 --> 00:18:02.120
B-B-But is that homemade?!

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:05.620
Y-Yeah, I-I think it's homemade.

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:07.580
--Ca-Ca-Ca-Ca-Ca...
--"Ca"?

00:18:07.790 --> 00:18:10.040
Ca-Can I see it?!

00:18:10.250 --> 00:18:13.710
Okay! Okay! Just stop shaking me!
I'm begging you!

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:18.180
--New Year's dishes?
--"New Year's dishes"?

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:22.430
--Would you like to see what's in the bottom box, too?
--W-W-W-Wait!

00:18:22.640 --> 00:18:23.810
I'm not mentally prepared yet!

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:25.230
Uh, okay...

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:28.850
I can't shake this sense of dread!
Sheer adrenaline has brought me this far,

00:18:29.060 --> 00:18:33.070
but if this is my chance to turn back,
I probably should take it...

00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:38.490
But... But... after coming this far, there really is no turning back!

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:40.490
Mr. Maou! Please open the bottom box!

00:18:40.700 --> 00:18:42.240
Y-Yes, Ma'am.

00:18:53.210 --> 00:18:54.880
Welcome!

00:18:56.170 --> 00:18:59.180
I spent another unexciting day stalking them...

00:19:00.470 --> 00:19:03.220
I tend to buy the same stuff every day without thinking, huh?

00:19:04.640 --> 00:19:08.690
Thank you very much.
Please shop with us again.

00:19:11.980 --> 00:19:14.070
Hm?! What just happened?!

00:19:15.570 --> 00:19:18.030
Sir? Are you okay?

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:19.320
Stay back!

00:19:25.160 --> 00:19:28.250
Stay inside! And call the police right away!

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:41.390
I don't know whether you're human or demon,

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:46.390
but why did you choose to attack me in a conspicuous place like this?!

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:48.140
It's one thing to come after me,

00:19:48.350 --> 00:19:52.230
but if you're trying to cause trouble for the people here, I'll show no mercy!

00:20:03.530 --> 00:20:06.030
What?! What happened?!

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:16.300
Take this!

00:20:19.210 --> 00:20:20.670
Stop!

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:23.340
Ah! Miss! Are you okay?!

00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:25.010
Are <i>you</i> okay?

00:20:25.220 --> 00:20:26.850
I'm sorry for pushing you away.

00:20:27.060 --> 00:20:28.430
Oh, I'm okay.

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:31.100
Really, I just hit my forehead, that's all.

00:20:31.310 --> 00:20:32.640
Did you call the police?

00:20:32.850 --> 00:20:37.940
I think an emergency alert went to the security company and the police.

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:40.280
--Oh, and, Miss...
--What is it?

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:43.280
I'm sorry, but the emergency manual states that

00:20:43.490 --> 00:20:47.490
we're to have the customers remain in the store until the police arrive.

00:20:47.700 --> 00:20:51.580
Could you wait until the police show up?

00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:01.340
It <i>is</i> working...

00:21:01.550 --> 00:21:04.340
The Better Half that I activated this time...

00:21:04.550 --> 00:21:10.560
It contained much stronger power than the time I fought Lucifer two months ago.

00:21:10.770 --> 00:21:14.310
With this power, I might even be able to use the Evil-Crushing Robe.

00:21:15.230 --> 00:21:19.980
But that just makes it harder to figure out what that purple light was.

00:21:20.190 --> 00:21:25.740
I've never encountered an enemy who nullified a sacred sword and celestial force.

00:21:25.950 --> 00:21:28.910
Excuse me, Miss! These are yours, right?

00:21:29.120 --> 00:21:31.450
Oh, sorry. Thanks.

00:21:35.670 --> 00:21:37.500
I-I like this music more than you'd think!

00:21:37.710 --> 00:21:38.840
Oh, I see.

00:21:39.040 --> 00:21:39.960
Miss Yusa!

00:21:40.170 --> 00:21:41.590
Huh? Chiho?!

00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:43.630
Miss Yusa! There's trouble!

00:21:43.840 --> 00:21:45.510
Chiho, what on Earth happened?

00:21:45.720 --> 00:21:48.680
Mr. Maou... Mr. Maou...!

00:21:48.890 --> 00:21:50.850
What happened to Maou?!

00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:55.350
Mr. Maou brought...!

00:21:55.560 --> 00:21:56.810
Wh-What did he bring?

00:21:57.020 --> 00:22:00.360
A-A-A heart mark with a lunch box that was in a homemade!

00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:03.490
A two-layered lady! Two-layered!

00:22:04.610 --> 00:22:05.650
Huh?

00:22:23.090 --> 00:22:28.470
<i>Where will morning start from, in this quiet sky?</i>

00:22:28.680 --> 00:22:34.100
<i>Fingertips twining in a pinky</i> <i>swear I pretended not to see</i>

00:22:34.310 --> 00:22:44.310
<i>If the moon's been laughed at,</i> <i>she'll sink away toward yesterday</i>

00:22:44.990 --> 00:22:50.240
<i>Liar, coward--if I'm all these things at once</i>

00:22:50.450 --> 00:22:55.950
<i>Then I only blossomed in dreams</i>

00:22:56.160 --> 00:23:01.500
<i>I hid in the moon's shadow,</i> <i>but the truth is, I was crying</i>

00:23:01.710 --> 00:23:07.220
<i>The tears won't flow anymore--</i> <i>did they all dry up?</i>

00:23:07.420 --> 00:23:13.760
<i>If I could forgive everything,</i> <i>maybe they'd flow again</i>

00:23:13.970 --> 00:23:21.310
<i>But these are all things I want to protect</i>

00:23:43.290 --> 00:23:45.920
"The Hero Enters the Fray"
